	"changenote" "[b]DynamicTrading Update: In-Game Manual System, Scavenger Radio Manual, and Documentation Improvements[/b]

[list]
[*] Implemented a full in-game manual system, enabling players to access colony, economy, NPC, and feature documentation directly within the game UI.
[*] Added Scavenger Radio manual, expanding player access to new in-game guides and related content.
[*] Enhanced update handling for the WhatsNew flow, including version tracking (releaseVersion/popupVersion) to prevent redundant prompts and ensure players see fresh notes when appropriate.
[*] Improved documentation formatting and consistency across manuals, with updates to reflect new versioning logic and clearer presentation.
[*] Strengthened configuration safety and UI state handling to improve robustness when navigating manuals.
[/list]"
	"title" "Dynamic Trading (w/ NPC) B42.13+"
	"description" "[h1]🔥 MASSIVE UPDATE: Dynamic Colonies, Labour & Admin Tools![/h1]
[list]
[] [b]Player Factions & Dynamic Colonies:[/b] Create and manage your own player-owned factions! Construct buildings like the new Infirmary, assign roles, and build a thriving community.
[] [b]Advanced Labour & Scavenging:[/b] Put your workers to use! Automate scavenging runs with a deep simulation that tracks worker tiredness, meal-based nutrition (HP), carry weight, and contextual map locations.
[] [b]In-Game Manual & Guides:[/b] Never get lost again. Access a fully searchable, dynamic in-game manual that provides detailed guides on World Events, the Economics Dashboard, Scavenger Radio, and Colony features.
[] [b]In-Game Price & Archetype Editor:[/b] Server admins can now dynamically configure the economy on the fly! Edit item prices, manage tags, adjust NPC item allocations, and force-generate traders directly through a dedicated in-game UI.
[] [b]Reputation System & NPC Interactions:[/b] Your actions have real consequences. A dynamic reputation system tracks your trade value, daily chats, and even player kills, directly influencing trader dialogue, relations, and faction standing.
[/list]
[hr][/hr]
[h1]THE DYNAMIC TRADING SYSTEM[/h1]
Transforms Project Zomboid’s economy into a living, breathing market. Prices fluctuate, traders move, and world events dictate value.
[list]
[] [b]Living Economy & Smart Pricing:[/b] A sophisticated tag-based pricing engine handles inflation and deflation. Item condition, rot, fluids per liter, and randomized durability all directly affect true market value.
[] [b]Events & Global Heat:[/b] Multi-flash events dynamically change the world. Winter spikes food prices; raids discount weapons.
[] [b]Realism Update:[/b] Traders sell scavenged goods with randomized durability, not factory-new products. However, producer archetypes (farmers, anglers, etc.) will still sell fresh produce depending on your luck!
[] [b]Medical Care & Needs:[/b] Hire Doctors, manage the new Infirmary building, and ensure your faction workers are healed and fed through the new tabbed warehouse supply UI.
[] [b]Wallets & Lottery:[/b] Zombies drop wallets—check them for cash and engage with the new wallet lottery system.
[/list]

[hr][/hr]
[h1]⚠️ CHOOSE YOUR VERSION (100% PARITY)[/h1]
[b]Both versions share the exact same advanced economy backend and can be swapped mid-save with NO issues![/b]
[b]Choose ONE. Do NOT enable both at the same time. Both require: [code]DynamicTradingCommon[/code][/b]

[h2]📻 OPTION A: Dynamic Trading V1 (Classic)[/h2]
[b]Mod ID:[/b][code]DynamicTrading[/code]
Best for players who want the deep simulated economy and colony management without physical NPCs and running around to get there.[list]
[] [b]Radio Only:[/b] Trade via Walkie-Talkies/HAM Radios.
[] [b]Scan Signals:[/b] Electricity skill helps find better signals.
[*] [b]Stable & Optimized:[/b] Fully server-authoritative networking with zero physical entities to impact performance.
[/list]

[h2]🧍‍♂️ OPTION B: Dynamic Trading V2[/h2]
[b]Mod ID:[/b] [code]DynamicTradingV2[/code]
A complete overhaul to V1. The economy physically exists in the world. Best for players who want realism and slightly harder gameplay due to them physically going to the Trader itself. You have been warned!
[list]
[] [b]Physical NPCs:[/b] Traders spawn, travel, rest, flee, and even become incapacitated! Features cyclical animations, ambient dialogue, and overhead health/name UIs.
[] [b]Factions & Reputation:[/b] Traders belong to groups with simulated wealth, goals, and shifting opinions of you based on interactions.
[] [b]Advanced Features:[/b] Core Quest System, Trader Management, Radar with distance sorting, and an all-new Faction UI dashboard.
[] [b]Optimized Performance:[/b] Spatial hashing and distance-aware network broadcasting ensures massive server bandwidth reductions.
[/list]

[hr][/hr][h1]📥 INSTALLATION[/h1]
[b]Classic (Radio):[/b] Enable [b]DynamicTradingCommon[/b] + [b]Dynamic Trading V1[/b]
[b]New (NPCs):[/b] Enable [b]DynamicTradingCommon[/b] + [b]Dynamic Trading V2[/b]
[b]✅ Safe to add/remove mid-save. Safe to swap between V1 and V2 at any time![/b]

[hr][/hr]
[h1]⏳ PLANNED ROADMAP[/h1]
[b]1. Player-Owned Storefronts:[/b] Construct a trading station at your base to automate sales to passing NPCs and earn passive income. (Partially Implimented in Dynamic Colonies)
[b]2. Expanded Contracts & Quests:[/b] Build upon the quest backend to fulfill high-priority faction requests (e.g., medical shortages) for massive reputation and cash bonuses.
[b]3. Crime & Consequence:[/b] The world fights back. Defend your wealth against burglars and rival factions, manage NPC sentiment, and hire [b]Guards[/b] to protect your stockpile.
[hr][/hr]
[h1]🏆 CREDITS & SUPPORT[/h1]
Thanks to [b]S4ro, IronLungs, External, Saren[/b] & the community.
[b]Like the mod? Rate it![/b]
